      "target": "../sections/sec-001-acknowledgements.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The National Health Workforce Accounts (NHWA) Handbook was developed under the direction of the World \nHealth Organization (WHO) Health Workforce Department to support the implementation of the Global Strategy \non Human Resources for Health: Workforce 2030.\nThe development of the NHWA Handbook version 2 was coordinated by the Data, Evidence and Knowledge \nManagement unit of the Health Workforce Department: Mourtala Abdou Illou, Mathieu Boniol, Khassoum Diallo, \nTeena Kunjumen, Maria Sarah Nabaggala, Tapas Sadasivan Nair, Amani Siyam. Special thanks to WHO colleagues \nwho provided contributions",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Acknowledgements: the handbook was developed under the direction of the WHO Health Workforce Department to support the Global Strategy on Human Resources for Health: Workforce 2030, and version 2 was coordinated by the department's Data, Evidence and Knowledge Management unit. It thanks named WHO contributors, the members of the Technical Expert Group convened for the revision, regional-office staff and national NHWA focal points from many countries who gave input in online consultations, and lists production coordination (Mathieu Boniol), editing and design.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
