    {
      "id": "library/9789240081291-eng/blocks/prose-sec-002",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Foreword",
      "pageStart": 11,
      "pageEnd": 12,
      "target": "../sections/sec-002-foreword.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Several years have passed since the launch of the National Health Workforce Accounts (NHWA) \nin 2017. And following a global pandemic that disrupted healthcare services worldwide, it is \nan opportune time to reflect on the progress, priorities, gaps, and adaptations of the NHWA. \nThe NHWA has witnessed unprecedented engagement from countries, partners, and all three \nlevels of the World Health Organization, with focal points nominated by most Member States \n(90%).\nThanks to collective efforts, there has been a significant improvement in the availability and \nquality of health workforce (HWF) d",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Foreword: since NHWA's launch in 2017, and after a pandemic that disrupted health services, it is time to reflect on its progress. Focal points have been nominated by 90% of Member States, and standardized measurement, streamlined reporting and multi-stakeholder involvement have improved the availability and quality of health workforce data, informing evidence on shortages, ageing, migration, gender and subnational inequalities, the workforce's COVID-19 role, and reports such as the State of the World's Nursing and Midwifery. New World Health Assembly resolutions and initiatives since 2017 recognize the centrality of the health and care workforce. The revision keeps continuity with NHWA v1.0 and its core principles — systems strengthening, progressive implementation, multi-sectoral governance, diversified data sources — while adapting to new priority data needs and adding more examples of data use.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-31"
      }
