      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Definition",
      "pageStart": 21,
      "pageEnd": 21,
      "target": "../sections/sec-011-definition.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The NHWA can be defined as – “a system by which countries progressively improve the \navailability, quality, and use of data on health workforce through monitoring of a set of indicators \nto support achievement of Universal Health Coverage, Sustainable Development Goals and \nother health objectives”.",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines NHWA as a system by which countries progressively improve the availability, quality and use of health workforce data by monitoring a set of indicators, to support UHC, the SDGs and other health objectives.",
