      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Implementation and use of the NHWA",
      "pageStart": 28,
      "pageEnd": 29,
      "target": "../sections/sec-016-implementation-and-use-of-the-nhwa.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Implementation and use of the NHWA\nImplementation of the NHWA\nThe NHWA contains indicators with clear policy relevance across the entire spectrum of HWF \npriorities and those related to the HLM framework. The implementation of the NHWA is a \ncountry-led activity, building on national systems and using existing mechanisms to coordinate \ndata-gathering for the evaluation of the HWF.\nWHO has developed a set of tools to help countries implement the NHWA. These include, \nin addition to this Handbook, an implementation guide (42) and an online platform for data \nreporting and visualization, as well",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Implementation and use of the NHWA: implementation is country-led, building on national systems and existing coordination mechanisms. WHO supports it with this Handbook, an implementation guide, an online reporting and visualization platform, and a public data portal publishing annually updated data as a global public good (Figure 5); regional offices and the Health Workforce Department (hrhstatistics@who.int) give direct support. NHWA has numeric and capability indicators (Part III), with policy-use examples in Part IV; the processes and units in indicator 4-02 (governance and leadership capacity) maximize policy use of the indicators, and indicator 4-05 addresses national capacity to monitor key planning and global-monitoring metrics.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
