      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Synthesis of indicators: tables giving, for each of the 29 NHWA v2 indicators, its number, short and full name, numerator, denominator and disaggregation. Module 1 (stock and flow) has 12: density per 10,000 (national and at the first subnational level), distribution by age group, sex, facility ownership, facility type, place of birth and place of training, annual inflow and outflow ratios (outflows by voluntary or involuntary exit), vacancy rate (funded full-time posts unfilled for at least twelve months over all funded posts) and distribution by full- or part-time contract; 'health workers' means all occupations in Annex 2, and population comes from UN World Population Prospects. Module 2 (education) has 7: training capacity per 10,000, applications to capacity, enrolments to applications, graduates to stock, programme duration, accreditation mechanisms, and standards for education and training with seven sub-indicators. Module 3 (finance) has 5: compensation expenditure, entry-level wages, education expenditure, expenditure per graduate and average tuition fee. Module 4 has 5: labour regulations and policies (12 sub-indicators, from working hours and minimum wage to attacks on health workers, mental well-being, CHW salaries and advanced nursing roles), governance and leadership capacity (5 sub-indicators), share of women in Ministry of Health senior management, IHR implementation capacity (rated None to Sustainable) and HRH information system capacity to monitor key metrics (9 sub-indicators).",
