      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "How to read indicator metadata",
      "pageStart": 49,
      "pageEnd": 51,
      "target": "../sections/sec-021-how-to-read-indicator-metadata.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The indicators in the NHWA are presented as metadata sheets. The indicators are mostly numeric \n(quantitative), i.e. representing in numbers certain ratios with a numerator and denominator \nrelated to a HRH policy field. There are also capability indicators on the existence of certain \nregulations, processes, etc. reflecting the status of development of the HRH management \nsystem of a country. The metadata sheets aim to provide a definition with explanations for the \nconnecting terms and methodology for the calculation. Definitions for key terms are presented \nin the Glossary, with an indicati",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "How to read indicator metadata: each indicator has a metadata sheet; most are numeric ratios with a numerator and denominator, and some are capability indicators on the existence of regulations or processes. Every sheet follows the same order: indicator number (module, then indicator), abbreviated and full name (with possible values such as Yes/Partial/No for categorical indicators), numerator and denominator (numeric indicators only), disaggregation, definition and technical notes (including capability questions and answer options), glossary terms, data reporting frequency (annual or every three years), potential data sources at national level in decreasing order of relevance, and further information and links.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-31"
      }
