      "target": "../sections/sec-042-2-07-standards-for-education-and-training-progra.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Indicator name\nExistence of standards for education and training programmes\nDefinition\nThis indicator is a composite of seven sub-indicators, see below. The response to these seven \nsub-indicators is aggregated as a score (see part II on methods) on a scale from 1 (nascent) to 5 \n(sustainable).\nEach sub-indicator is a self-assessment of one aspect of standards on education and training \nprogrammes. To help answer these self-assessed sub-indicators, a series of guiding questions  \nare provided.\nSub-indicator \n2 – 07.1\nExistence of national and/or subnational standards for social accountability",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Metadata sheet for indicator 2-07, standards for education and training programmes: a composite of seven self-assessed sub-indicators aggregated into a score on a scale from 1 (nascent) to 5 (sustainable), each with guiding questions — standards for social accountability, including civil-society and community involvement in accreditation (2-07.1); social determinants of health in standards and curricula (2-07.2); interprofessional education (2-07.3); cooperation between institutions and regulators on accreditation standards (2-07.4); national continuing professional development systems, whether compulsory and linked to re-licensure (2-07.5); in-service training within national education plans (2-07.6); and standards for community health worker curricula, reported as not applicable where a country has no CHWs (2-07.7). Disaggregated by programme except for 2-07.7, and reported every three years for the Global Strategy, SDNM, the PHC Measurement Framework and CHW guidance, from ministries of health, education and labour, accreditation authorities, statutory bodies and professional registers.",
