      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Opening of Module 4, Working conditions, governance and leadership: the module looks from three perspectives. The first indicator asks how well regulations and policies protect health workers; the second and third, from the national leadership side, look at mechanisms to coordinate the HRH agenda, including promoting women in leadership; the IHR indicator assesses workforce availability for emergency preparedness and response in line with the existing monitoring framework; and the last assesses capacity to report key metrics for frameworks mostly adopted by World Health Assembly resolutions. As national-level assessments covering all health and care workers, these indicators carry no disaggregation.",
