    {
      "id": "library/9789240081291-eng/blocks/prose-sec-054",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "+ Part IV: Examples of how to use NHWA to inform policy development",
      "pageStart": 91,
      "pageEnd": 93,
      "target": "../sections/sec-054-part-iv-examples-of-how-to-use-nhwa-to-inform-po.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "NHWA to inform policy \ndevelopment\nNational health workforce accounts: a handbook – second edition\n78\nThis section illustrates how the NHWA indicators could be combined and used to inform the \ndevelopment of policies for HCWs. Each of the following HWF topics can receive a specific \nin-depth study within a HLM analysis (68), in which all NHWA indicators could be relevant, and \nfor which additional studies and data might be required. However, once these main policies \nare identified as priority for the country, a regular monitoring on selected indicators would be \nrequired. Time-trend analysis",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Introduction to Part IV, Examples of how to use NHWA to inform policy development: it shows how NHWA indicators can be combined to inform policies for health and care workers. Each topic could warrant an in-depth health labour market analysis drawing on all indicators and further data, but once a policy is a national priority, selected indicators should be monitored regularly, with time trends showing whether the challenge is improving or new policies are needed; each topic is presented to help countries choose indicators for routine follow-up.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-31"
      }
